{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794179837,"nonce":"jdBlqHXb1BxIsl3K0+f6E3sPWoY=","title":"Class styles lost after VisualOnly and LayoutChanged incremental updates","message":"GitHub issue #70.\n\nAn incremental update replaces node props in place with the new element tree's\nprops, which carry no style from class selectors. In\n`windowed/event_loop/frame/rebuild.rs`, the \"Normal incremental update\" branch\nre-applied the stylesheet's base styles only for `ChildrenChanged`. After a\n`VisualOnly` or `LayoutChanged` update (a button changing its colour, say),\nevery element whose background or text colour came from a class rule fell back\nto defaults: black window, default font.\n\nReproducer: a tree with a `.panel` class background; change only a neighbour's\ncolour or width; the panel loses its red background.\n\nFix in PR #71: `restyle_after_incremental_update(tree, result)` applies the base\nstyles for every result that changed props (`VisualOnly`, `LayoutChanged`,\n`ChildrenChanged`), and the layout overrides where layout is recomputed.\n`NoChanges` does nothing.\n\nTests: `class_background_survives_a_visual_only_update`,\n`class_background_survives_a_layout_changed_update`,\n`incremental_update_alone_drops_the_class_background` (shows the defect without\nthe call). Also reproduced and checked in a real window with real input\n(nested KWin).","files":null}]}